    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following the spec, and wrote 33 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (33 passed). I did not measure line coverage, because the only permitted command was the plain test run. Every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by a test, so I expect the 90% gate to pass, but that is unconfirmed. The implementation validates line items first, then checks coupon validity (unknown kind, expiry, prior use, minimum subtotal), then the coupon's value range, applies the discount capped at the subtotal, and adds shipping of 10.00 when the discounted subtotal is below 100.00 (or 0 for an empty order). The result is quantized to cents with ROUND_HALF_UP. Where the spec was silent I made these choices: `bool` quantities are rejected as non-integers, and a coupon is checked for validity before its value range. Three of my initial test expectations were wrong (they forgot that a discounted subtotal below 100 still pays shipping), so I corrected them; the implementation was right.",
